    `Father, I receive today the most extraordinary truth about who You are — that You are the God who comes down. Not the distant sovereign who observes from above and sends instructions. The God who descended — into the garden, into the bush, into the womb, into the tomb. Who came all the way to the bottom so that the bottom would never again be a place where You are absent. Let me live today from the awareness of a God who has come down — who is not far from any one of us, who does not need to be persuaded to be present, who has already made the descent and who therefore meets me in the lowest places of my life not as a visitor but as One who knows the terrain from the inside. You came down. You are here. That is enough.`
