    prayers: [
    `Father, I receive today Your patience — not as the evidence that You do not care, not as the permission to continue in what needs to change, but as the most active and most costly form of love available: the willingness to wait, to hold the door open, to renew the mercy every morning rather than closing the account on the basis of what yesterday produced. Let Your kindness lead me to repentance today — in whatever area the kindness has been patient with me longest, in whatever place the newness of the mercy this morning is the most undeserved. Your mercies are new. Your faithfulness is great. Your patience toward me is not slowness. It is love that has decided not to give up. Great is Your faithfulness. Let me live today like I believe it.`
    ],
