    `Father, I receive today the theology of the grain of wheat — the truth that the breaking is not the end of the fruitfulness but its beginning, that the burial is not the defeat of the purpose but the condition of its fulfilment. Where I have been resisting the breaking, interpreting it as destruction rather than as the releasing of what You put inside me for this very purpose, give me the faith of the grain that trusts the ground. I bring You the specific brokenness I am currently carrying — the cracked jar, the wounded hip, the thing that has not gone the way I planned. And I receive from John 12:24 the truth that the dying is the condition of the much fruit, not its cancellation. Let the breaking release what the intact shell was containing. A broken and contrite heart You will not despise. Here is mine.`
